# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots apache (with the Shellshock-vulnerable bash in place
# for its CGIs) and then execs `sleep infinity`, so the CGI attack surface is
# live when the agent starts and PID 1 is stable across an apache restart.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix is to restore a patched bash
# (apt-get install --reinstall bash). No apache restart is required - mod_cgi
# forks a fresh bash per request, so the patched binary takes effect immediately.
